---
// User-selected typographic mosaic: compact, passive, and slowly repeating.
// Areas are illustrative relative referent weights. Mention changes ink only.
---
<figure class="spacefig" data-space tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="spacefig-title" aria-describedby="spacefig-description">
  <div class="spacefig-heading">
    <span id="spacefig-title">What <i>animal</i> leaves open</span><span>Fig. 1</span>
  </div>
  <div class="spacefig-context" aria-hidden="true">
    <p data-line="0">“There is an animal.”</p>
    <p data-line="1">“It is in the tree.”</p>
    <p data-line="2">“It <em>might</em> be an insect.”</p>
  </div>
  <div class="spacefig-field-heading" aria-hidden="true"><span>Four example candidates</span><span>area: relative weight</span></div>
  <div class="spacefig-field" data-field aria-hidden="true">
    <canvas></canvas>
    <div class="spacefig-region" data-kind="bird"><span class="spacefig-name">BIRD</span></div>
    <div class="spacefig-region" data-kind="dog"><span class="spacefig-name">DOG</span></div>
    <div class="spacefig-region" data-kind="monkey"><span class="spacefig-name">MONKEY</span></div>
    <div class="spacefig-region" data-kind="insect"><span class="spacefig-name" data-mentioned>INSECT</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="spacefig-note"><span class="spacefig-ink-key">Warm ink: explicitly mentioned.</span> Illustrative weights, not measurements.</p>
  <p class="sr-only" id="spacefig-description">
    A slow, repeating illustration with four example candidates, not all animals. Bird, dog, monkey and insect
    remain possible referents. The context “in the tree” redistributes their illustrative relative weights.
    “It might be an insect” then makes insect bold and warm-coloured without changing its area.
    The animation pauses while keyboard-focused or while its tab is hidden. Reduced-motion preferences show the mentioned state.
  </p>
  <figcaption>
    <b>Fig. 1</b> What a description leaves open, and what it makes explicit:
    <a href="/research/typicality-in-referent-choice"><i>Typicality in referent choice</i></a>
    and <a href="/research/three-ways"><i>Three Ways of Leaving p Unsettled</i></a>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
  import "../scripts/space-figure.js";
</script>
<style>
  .spacefig { --space-ink:#282825; --space-warm:#9b4d2e; margin:1.6rem 0 0; color:var(--space-ink); }
  .spacefig-heading { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:12px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border-strong); padding-bottom:8px; font:12px/1.4 var(--font-mono); }
  .spacefig-heading > span:last-child { color:var(--color-text-muted); }
  .spacefig-context { display:grid; gap:2px; margin:12px 0; font:13px/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .spacefig-context p { margin:0; min-height:20px; }
  .spacefig-context p:not(:first-child) { opacity:.12; }
  .spacefig-context p { font-weight:600; transition:opacity .25s ease,color .25s ease; }
  .spacefig-context p.is-current { color:#282825!important; font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline; text-decoration-color:var(--color-border-strong); text-underline-offset:4px; }
  .spacefig-context p[data-line="2"] { color:#9b4d2e; }
  .spacefig-context p.is-current[data-line="2"] { color:#9b4d2e!important; text-decoration-color:#9b4d2e; }
  .spacefig-context em { font-style:normal; }
  .spacefig-field-heading { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:8px; margin-bottom:6px; color:#62625c; font:12px/1.4 var(--font-mono); }
  .spacefig-field { position:relative; height:196px; border-top:1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); isolation:isolate; overflow:hidden; }
  .spacefig-field canvas { display:block; position:absolute; inset:0; width:100%; height:100%; }
  .spacefig-region { position:absolute; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; pointer-events:none; }
  .spacefig-name { display:block; background:var(--color-bg); padding:4px 9px; font:400 19px/1.1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing:.08em; white-space:nowrap; }
  .spacefig-note { margin:9px 0 0; font:12px/1.5 var(--font-mono); color:#62625c; }
  .spacefig-ink-key { color:var(--space-warm); }
  .spacefig figcaption { font-size:.86rem; line-height:1.5; color:var(--color-text-muted); margin-top:8px; }
  .spacefig figcaption b { margin-right:5px; font:500 12px var(--font-mono); color:var(--color-text); }
  .spacefig figcaption a { color:var(--color-accent); }
  .spacefig:focus-visible { outline:1px solid var(--color-border-strong); outline-offset:8px; }
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce) { .spacefig-context p { transition:none; } }
  @media(max-width:600px) {
    .spacefig { margin-top:1.4rem; }
    .spacefig-field { height:184px; }
    .spacefig-field-heading { flex-wrap:wrap; row-gap:2px; }
    .spacefig-name { font-size:16px; letter-spacing:.025em; padding:3px 6px; }
    .spacefig-note { font-size:12px; }
  }
</style>
